Jahshaka patch 0036 — a screen-space reflection REPLACES the environment term
it supersedes; it never adds to it.

WHY (lane SSR-1, 2026-09-14, defect C of the owner's push #34 smoke). Upstream
composites SSR into the specular environment term two different ways, chosen by
a DATABLOCK property:

    @property( use_envprobe_map )
        pixelData.envColourS = lerp( pixelData.envColourS.xyz,
                                     ssrReflection.xyz, ssrReflection.w );
    @else
        pixelData.envColourS += ssrReflection.xyz * ssrReflection.w;
    @end

The lerp is the physics: `pixelData.envColourS` and the screen-space trace are
two ESTIMATES OF ONE INTEGRAL — the radiance arriving along the specular lobe —
and `ssrReflection.w` is how much of that integral the screen was able to answer
for. What the screen answered, the probe must not answer again.

The `@else` is not a second opinion about that, it is an accident of which
property happens to be set. `use_envprobe_map` is raised in
`HlmsPbs::notifyPropertiesMergedPreGenerationStep` only for a datablock with its
own reflection cubemap or one covered by parallax-corrected cubemaps — but three
other things write `pixelData.envColourS` BEFORE this line and none of them
raises it: `applyVoxelConeTracing` (the voxel cone's specular), `applyIrradianceField`
and `applyIrradianceVolumes`. So a scene lit by VCT or the irradiance field with
no sky cube and no probe grid — which is an ordinary configuration in this
editor, and the one a sealed room with Photon at medium produces — shades every
mirror as "the screen's answer PLUS the voxel cone's answer for the same
directions". That is the same lobe counted twice, and on a near-mirror surface
the second copy is the whole reflection again.

IT COMPOUNDS, because this renderer's SSR is a closed loop: the shaded colour is
copied into the history the next frame's resolve reads (OgreChain.cpp kSsrPrev),
so a doubled reflection is re-reflected doubled. The energy the owner metered on
a mirror floor is this series, not a brighter reflection.

WHY IT CANNOT MOVE A SHIPPED FRAME. Where `envColourS` is zero at this line the
two spellings are the same arithmetic: lerp(0, R, w) == 0 + R*w, exactly, with
no rounding to argue about. Where it is NOT zero the old code was double-counting
by construction. And every scene that has a sky or probes already took the lerp
branch: OgreSky.cpp binds the IBL cube as PBSM_REFLECTION on every material when
no automatic PCC is bound, and the PCC path sets `parallax_correct_cubemaps` when
it is — either way `use_envprobe_map` is 1. Measured: the Mirror Room, the
ShadowMapFromCode port and the default scene are bit-identical across this patch,
and `--engine-selftest` keeps its hash.

MEDIA-ONLY: Studio stages this file from the ogre-next SOURCE tree
(cmake/IncludeOgre.cmake), so every tree needs the patch loop, but no engine
rebuild.

A TRAP THIS PATCH FELL INTO FIRST, recorded because the symptom is far from the
cause: the Hlms template parser reads `@property`, `@else` and `@end` ANYWHERE in
the text, comments included. The first version of the comment below wrote
"Upstream's @else branch", which the parser took as a real directive, unbalanced
the surrounding block and emitted a shader that failed to compile a thousand
lines away ("'branch' : undeclared identifier") for SOME property permutations
only — with VCT on here, so the fixture rendered black. Never write an @keyword
in a comment inside a .any file.

And the file is CRLF, which is load-bearing for THIS FILE TOO: the hunk below
carries the target's carriage returns, so the patch applies with a plain
`git apply` and needs no `--ignore-whitespace`. The first round of this patch
lost them by round-tripping the .patch through Python's text mode (round 2 of
lane SSR-1 caught it: `--check` then failed on a tree carrying 0001-0035 and
`build-ogre.sh` would have exited 1 at every pull). Verified BOTH WAYS on every
revision: `git apply --check` against a tree with 0001-0035 applied, and
`git apply --reverse --check` against the lane's own patched submodule.

--- a/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any
+++ b/Samples/Media/Hlms/Pbs/Any/Main/800.PixelShader_piece_ps.any
@@ -992,11 +992,21 @@
